<title>USA: Vermont Aug unemployment rate drifts up to 4.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Vermont Aug unemployment rate drifts up to 4.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vermont said on Tuesday that the state unemployment rate edged up 0.1 percentage point to 4.3 percent in August, as the number of unemployed hit the highest level in a year despite the usual summer hirings.</p>
<p>On an unseasonally adjusted basis, unemployment rates for the state's 13 labor markets ranged from 1.7 percent in Hartford-Lebanon to 7.1 percent in Newport.</p>
<p>&quot;Unemployment continued to drift higher due partly to the relatively modest job growth in recent months,&quot; said Susan Auld, Commissioner of the state Department of Employment and Training, in prepared remarks.</p>
<p>The following are some of the highlights of the state's report.  </p>
<p>--Total, all industries, 275.3, up 0.4 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Total, private, 230.7, up 0.3 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Construction, 13.2, up 0.1 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Mining, 0.6, unchanged from July 1996</p>
<p>--Manufacturing, 46.4, up 0.1 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Durable Goods, 30.7, up 0.3 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Nondurable Goods, 15.7, down 0.2 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Transportation &amp; Public Utilities, 11.8, unchanged from</p>
<p>	   July 1996</p>
<p>--Wholesale Trade, 13.1, up 0.1 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Retail Trade, 52.4, up 0.3 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Financial, Insurance and Real Estate, 12.5, up 0.2 from</p>
<p>	   July 1996</p>
<p>--Services 80.7, down 0.5 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Government, 44.6, up 0.1 from July 1996</p>
<p>--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654</p>
